      "file": "lubricating_oil_skid_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Clean, cool oil at controlled pressure",
      "description": "The main pump delivers more oil than the machine needs; the pressure-control valve spills the excess back to the reservoir to hold header pressure (typically ≈ 1–2.5 bar(g) at the bearings). Coolers keep supply ≈ 40–50 °C; duplex filters (≈ 10 µm) can be switched on-line. The standby pump starts automatically on falling pressure, and the accumulator / rundown tank covers the switch-over and coast-down so bearings are never starved.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
